        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Review result: incomplete—event records require authorized access\n\nI verified the relevant work order and Pending Close cutoff, but **cannot determine whether a late-created event occurred from the records authorized for this assignment**. The supporting event records returned an access-denied response; I requested an authorized release rather than relying on unverified data.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation / product | Modine Racine–Dekoven / Cooler Plate Pack |\n| Cost period | **Sep-25**, `PER-COST-2025-09` |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **2025-09-30T18:00:00** — timezone not specified in the source |\n| Source transaction ID | Not verified |\n| Event amount | Not verified |\n| Exact event-created time | Not verified |\n| Minutes after Pending Close | Cannot calculate without the authorized event timestamp |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not verified |\n| Status consistent with Oracle policy? | **Undetermined** |\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B states that newly created transactions falling in or before a **Pending Close** period are not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting; they are processed after the period is closed or reopened. Transactions entered before Pending Close continue processing, including those in error. **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions that continue processing.**\n\nThus, a newly created, non-exempt event after the cutoff should be held rather than processed. Applying that rule to this work order requires the event’s type, creation timestamp, and recorded status.\n\n**Sources:** `state.db`, authorized `work_orders` and `cost_periods` records; Oracle documentation, “Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 / printed page 225.\n\nNo database records were changed. The partial audit and provenance were saved to `/cache/work/worker_e7b6e3dc8005/audit-report.json`; the submitted report remains marked **needs evidence**.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
